{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3103","published":"2026-07-24T11:11:59Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:21.347134743Z","upstream":["CVE-2022-36648"],"summary":"qemu security update","details":"QEMU is a FAST! processor emulator using dynamic translation to achieve good emulation speed.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nThe hardware emulation in the of_dpa_cmd_add_l2_flood of rocker device model in QEMU, as used in 7.0.0 and earlier, allows remote attackers to crash the host qemu and potentially execute code on the host via execute a malformed program in the guest OS. Note: This has been disputed by multiple third parties as not a valid vulnerability due to the rocker device not falling within the virtualization use case.(CVE-2022-36648)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qemu","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qemu&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qemu-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-curl-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-iscsi-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-rbd-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-ssh-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debuginfo-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debugsource-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-guest-agent-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-hw-usb-host-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-img-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-aarch64-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-arm-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-riscv-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-x86_64-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-binfmt-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-static-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["qemu-help-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["qemu-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["qemu-8.2.0-57.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","qemu-block-curl-8.2